// The bits a store of `e` into a name adds when `e` is not a list literal
// (esc_fresh, store.id): 0 for a string literal, which a string owner copies to
// the heap when it stores it; 16 for a fresh string (a concat, or a builtin
// that makes one), which gives a string name something to free; 2 for anything
// else, whose value may be held by another name.
esc_nonlit(int e) {
  int r = 2;
  if((import nkind)[e] == "str") {
    r = 0;
  } else if(str_fresh_node(e) == 1) {
    r = 16;
  }
} return int r;
